        "heading_wYhaAR": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What Are the Benefits and Applications of Gaffer’s Tape?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_HMmcEk": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Gaffer’s tape is a heavy, pressure-sensitive cloth tape with a strong yet easy-to-remove adhesive backing. Used in everything from industrial staging to filmmaking and photography, this versatile cotton tape has a matte finish that is ideal for visually concealing cords as well as vibrant coloring options for labeling or marking. Gaffer’s tape is also helpful for temporarily securing cables that would otherwise be a tripping hazard. Its many advantageous properties lend it to high-performance uses in a variety of applications.</p>",
            "text_size": "text-base"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_wYhaAR",
        "text_HMmcEk"
      ],
