    "image_with_text_kKKhWk": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_4PQMHn": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Benefits and Applications",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_xWAFd3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Gaffer’s tape, or gaff tape, has a unique combination of attributes that differentiate it from other adhesive options. These include:</p><ul><li><strong>Durability. </strong>Gaffer’s tape can handle heavy foot and equipment traffic without wearing down.</li><li><strong>Heat tolerance.</strong> Gaffer’s tape can withstand relatively high temperatures without melting, making it ideal for tolerating heat from light fixtures and other equipment.<br/></li></ul><p>These benefits make gaffer’s tape an excellent adhesive option for filmmaking, theater, and music applications, as well as many industrial and domestic tasks. Examples of applications include:</p><ul><li><strong>Managing cables, wires, and extension cords.</strong> From industrial spaces to filmmaking sets, gaffer’s tape is ideal for securing wires and cables to the floor for safety, connecting multiple cables together, or hiding them from the sightline of an audience or camera.</li><li><strong>Affixing items to surfaces.</strong> Gaffer’s tape provides a reliable solution for securely affixing paper, cloth, backdrops, props, and other items to walls or floors. Also, the filmmaking industry often uses it to attach gels to lighting rigs or secure spikes to tripods.</li><li><strong>Labeling items and marking positions.</strong> Compatible with various surface types, gaffer’s tape is great for labeling everything from cameras and accessories to dimmers and circuits. Users can also apply it to the floor to mark an actor’s standing position or indicate where a prop should be.</li><li><strong>Repairing.</strong> The durability and strong adhesive properties of gaffer’s tape make it suitable for repairing tears in vinyl surfaces such as seat coverings and equipment covers.</li></ul>",
            "subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_4PQMHn",
        "text_xWAFd3"
      ],
