    "image_with_text_PxGWXk": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_wrWb4X": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What Is the Difference Between Gaffer’s Tape and Duct Tape?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_DTeqzm": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>While both gaffer’s tape and duct tape are multi-purpose, pressure-sensitive cloth tapes, they each offer several distinct properties and benefits that impact their suitability for certain uses. For example, duct tape features a durable polyethylene coating on top of the cloth layer, which provides superior flexibility and stretching capabilities for sticking to textured or uneven surfaces. These features make this rubber-based adhesive exceptionally strong and versatile. </p><p>Other key differences between gaffer’s tape and duct tape include:</p><ul><li><strong>Adhesive properties.</strong> While duct tape’s aggressive adhesive properties make it great for permanent or semi-permanent applications, it can be difficult to remove without damaging or tearing the underlying surface. Gaffer’s tape, on the other hand, is well suited for temporary applications that require easy, quick removal with little or no residue left behind.</li><li><strong>Ease of handling. </strong>While most types of duct tape are relatively easy to tear by hand, certain types have extra reinforcements and require cutting with scissors or other tools. In comparison, users can easily hand-tear gaffer’s tape along its width and length.</li><li><strong>Resistance to heat and water.</strong> Duct tape’s waterproof and weather-resistant polyethylene coating makes it great for heavy-use and outdoor applications. However, exposure to high heat can interfere with the tape’s integrity, eventually causing it to fail. Although gaffer’s tape lacks this waterproof coating, it provides good moisture resistance and is less susceptible to melting than duct tape. </li></ul>",
            "subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_wrWb4X",
        "text_DTeqzm"
      ],
